  "notes": "Fix the cold-presence check for sparse loaded-sensor readings by extending its bounded observation window from 300 ms to 430 ms, so the check can collect the required samples before deciding whether presence is confirmed.\n\nWhen automatic IR sensor initialization is lost, request a SensorLoss stop in the affected modes instead of continuing without the sensor. Offline host regression coverage shows the old path fails and the updated path requests a stop in all three modes. The reported physical incident's cause remains unconfirmed.\n\nThis release is host-validated for beta field testing. Native installation, physical sensor-stop behavior, smoke testing, and physical acceptance remain pending because the device was disconnected from USB for the user's requested Wi-Fi field testing. These notes do not claim device-level proof.\n\nThis is a binary-only package. It includes the application image and filesystem; no HW1 source code or source repository commit is published or claimed.",
